{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Breakdown of the 874 unsigned events (2026-11-19 PST, rebar-session-3d705fec)\n\nMeasured on a no-remote clone of origin/tickets 37033c41613 (311,172 commits; `--git-dir` is its own `.git`). Same scope rule as enforced `verify-identity --all`: 51,049 events in scope, 874 unsigned. All 874 are raw event files at HEAD; none is a SNAPSHOT ledger entry. They span 346 tickets (170 bug, 101 story, 64 task, 11 epic; 342 closed). Types: LINK 233, SIGNATURE 181, EDIT 175, STATUS 147, COMMENT 118, FILE_IMPACT 19, UNLINK 1.\n\nEvery signer in this store signs as identity 594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d. Its keyring: PU4nHIqJCR (added 2026-07-13), oGCqzgfDMp (added 2026-09-07 15:39 PDT), va7mtsoMZ4 (added 2026-11-19 09:47 PST); none revoked.\n\nGroups and why each is unsigned (the write seam `_commands/_seam.py::_apply_authorship` signs only when the event has an `author_id` AND a signing key is configured; otherwise it logs a warning and writes unsigned):\n1. **621 events: operator Mac checkout (env 492a5c71), author_id 594c, 2026-09-24 22:08 PDT to 2026-11-04 02:49 PST.** No signing key was configured in that environment. The key file `~/.config/rebar/rebar-bot-signing-key` (oGCqzgfDMp) dates from 2026-11-02 13:18 PST; the first signed event from this env is 2026-11-04 04:23 PST, and none is unsigned after that.\n2. **209 LINK events: review-bot box (env b2b5c498), author \"Unknown\", no author_id, 2026-07-19 to 2026-08-09 PDT.** The bot had no resolved identity, so signing was skipped; the same box also lacked ssh-keygen (fixed by beb1, a7871c95457, 2026-08-09).\n3. **44 events with no author_id from interactive sessions:** 30 \"rebar review bot\" + 4 \"Joe Oakhart\" + 1 \"Unknown\" on env 492a5c71 (2026-09-16 to 09-21 PDT); 8 \"Joe Oakhart\" on env b8a354e0 (2026-08-23/24 PDT); 1 \"RebarBotNava\" on env ade0f2ef (2026-08-01 PDT). No identity resolved for the writer, so signing was skipped.\n\nTiming: 218 predate oGCqzgfDMp's KEY_ADD (2026-09-07); 310 fall below the 30-day horizon (~2026-10-20), 564 above it.\n\nConsequences for remediation (from verify_authorship.py and authorship.py):\n- `enforce_since` re-anchoring cannot reduce the unsigned count: `verify-identity` counts verdicts before grandfathering, and the hold check runs with no `enforce_since`.\n- Compaction omits unsigned events from the SNAPSHOT `authorship_ledger` (`compact_txn._build_authorship_ledger`), so folding them removes them from scope. That hides them; it does not make them verifiable.\n- A live event with no `author_id` classifies `unknown-author` even when signed. `author_id` is inside the signed content hash, so the 253 events in groups 2 and 3 cannot verify without changing their recorded content.\n- An era-valid signature needs a key whose KEY_ADD precedes the event's introducing commit. For the 218 pre-2026-09-07 events that is PU4nHIqJCR, whose private half is not on this machine. Signing them with oGCqzgfDMp would yield `key_not_valid_at_era`.\n- Only group 1 (621) can be made genuinely verifiable: author_id 594c is recorded, and oGCqzgfDMp was valid at every one of their commits. That needs a retroactive signature with that key, and the signature changes the reducer's per-ticket `authorship` signed/unsigned counts."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795124045173138001,"uuid":"1e9d83d0-0a21-4b31-bbd6-e1274064d3b7"}